From 139631b3ea18b5c21216ec094c0647198d40f5c7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Hughes <ryan@heyoodle.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 19:18:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1071/1072] usb: typec: ucsi: acpi: query the _DSM functions
 before using them

The ACPI specification has callers evaluate _DSM function 0 to learn
which functions are implemented before calling any. ucsi_acpi has never
done so, and calls the write and read functions directly.

Firmware can depend on the query. On the ASUS ProArt P14 (NVIDIA N1x)
it opens the EC's UCSI service over FF-A; without it the EC never acts
on the commands written through function 1, so the PPM reset times out
and the driver fails to probe on every boot:

  ucsi_acpi USBC000:00: failed to reset PPM!
  ucsi_acpi USBC000:00: error -ETIMEDOUT: PPM init failed

Query the functions before registering. A firmware that does not report
them is only noted, as before the driver used them unconditionally.
---
 drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_acpi.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_acpi.c b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_acpi.c
index 18286d3e9c..f11feb7077 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_acpi.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/ucsi/ucsi_acpi.c
@@ -219,6 +219,16 @@ static int ucsi_acpi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	ua->dev = &pdev->dev;
 
+	/*
+	 * Query the supported _DSM functions before calling any, as the ACPI
+	 * specification asks callers to. Firmware may rely on it: on the ASUS
+	 * ProArt P14 (NVIDIA N1x) the query opens the EC's UCSI service, and
+	 * without it the PPM never completes its reset.
+	 */
+	if (!acpi_check_dsm(ACPI_HANDLE(&pdev->dev), &ua->guid, 1,
+			    BIT(UCSI_DSM_FUNC_WRITE) | BIT(UCSI_DSM_FUNC_READ)))
+		dev_dbg(&pdev->dev, "_DSM does not report the UCSI read/write functions\n");
+
 	id = dmi_first_match(ucsi_acpi_quirks);
 	if (id)
 		ops = id->driver_data;
-- 
